{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261112T023812Z-931ea016", "ts": "2026-11-12T02:41:06Z", "actor": {"worktree": "pool-only", "plugin": "3.8.1-dev", "branch": "chore/pool-only"}, "body": {"base_commit": "ecdeff4820dbef96e1b52d2d33c59f8d45ccc42d", "base_tree": "4011f4ebd6120c799c4b7b70a3e4daf4affe6cfb", "head_tree": "a6c645671f3b28990f814f410c384c00019a975a", "head_commit": null, "dispatch_commit": "ecdeff4820dbef96e1b52d2d33c59f8d45ccc42d", "mode": "chunk (lighter pass, not ready for push)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "inner", "tier": "standard", "roster": [{"role": "reviewer", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": [".testament.toml", "CHANGELOG.md", "CLAUDE.md", "docs/testing.md", "scripts/test.sh", "tests/test_test_sh_script.py"], "files_changed": [".testament.toml", "CHANGELOG.md", "CLAUDE.md", "docs/testing.md", "scripts/test.sh", "tests/test_test_sh_script.py"], "files_oracle": [], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "blocking", "title": "-s, --capture=no, --pdb and --trace still run a whole package or the whole suite on the laptop: pool-only does not stop them, and test.sh lets them through", "recommendation": "class: testament's guide (guide-project.md:97-100) says that under fallback = \"pool-only\" a flag that needs the terminal (--pdb, -s, --co) still runs on this machine. test.sh flags only -x/--maxfail/--lf/--ff/--sw/-n and the -x bundles (scripts/test.sh:140-151), so `./scripts/test.sh core -vs` runs all of core on the laptop and `./scripts/test.sh -s` runs all ~53k tests there. That is the load the owner asked to end, and it contradicts the new CLAUDE.md:155 ('hands the run to testament's runners ..., and only there') and the CHANGELOG headline ('the laptop runs tests only on purpose'). Fix: give test.sh one list of everything testament keeps local, taken from testament's documented sets: -s, --capture=no, --capture no, --pdb, --trace, plus short bundles that hold s (e.g. -vs, -sx). Apply the same rule as -x to all of it: named test files run locally, anything wider is refused with exit 2. --co/--collect-only can stay as they are, since they run no tests. Add one parametrized test per member.", "files": ["scripts/test.sh", "CLAUDE.md", "CHANGELOG.md", "docs/testing.md"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "blocking", "title": "New routing branches have no test: --area with named files and a local-process flag is refused, and an environment gate with -x stays local", "recommendation": "instance: scripts/test.sh:179-182 adds a refusal (exit 2, 'select on the testament pool, and <flag> keeps this run local') that no test reaches, because every TestFlagsThatNeedOneLocalProcess case omits --area/--not-area. The guard `-z \"$local_only\"` at scripts/test.sh:173 is also what keeps `RECORD=1 ./scripts/test.sh core -x` running locally rather than being refused, and test_a_chosen_local_run_keeps_them has no env-gate case. Add `['evals', _EVALS_FILE, '--area', 'evals', '-x']` -> returncode 2, argv == [], that message; and an env-gate param ({'RECORD': '1'}, True) on test_a_chosen_local_run_keeps_them.", "files": ["scripts/test.sh", "tests/test_test_sh_script.py"], "fid": "R-2"}], "counts": {"blocking": 2, "warning": 0, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "docs/testing.md:154-156 still says a local test.sh pool run sends loop_timing to the pool", "recommendation": "instance: the manifest now excludes loop_timing, so this sentence is false and contradicts the same file's lines 80-81. Delete 'A local `test.sh` pool run still sends them to the pool;' and keep the ci-unit-tests.sh --loop-timing pointer. Accept or batch.", "files": ["docs/testing.md"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "docs/testing.md:33 still lists `-m` among the runs that go local and refuse areas", "recommendation": "instance: TestDashMGoesToThePool::test_with_areas now proves `--not-area evals -m slow` goes to testament. Delete `-m` from that list. Accept or batch.", "files": ["docs/testing.md"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "CI comments still describe the manifest's marker as `not integration`", "recommendation": "instance: scripts/ci-unit-pool.sh:7-9 and :38-40 (the narrowed `(not integration) and (not loop_timing)` example) and .github/workflows/ci.yml:62 describe the old expression. The pool run's `-m \"not loop_timing\"` is now redundant but harmless. Make the comments relational ('the manifest's expression') or delete the example. Outside this diff; accept or batch.", "files": ["scripts/ci-unit-pool.sh", ".github/workflows/ci.yml"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "The -x bundle check misses -x bundled with value-taking short options; several flag forms are untested", "recommendation": "instance: test.sh lets `-xrs`, `-vxrs` and `-xkfoo` through to testament (the guard at test.sh:148 admits only [vqslx]). Under pool-only testament then exits 2 (usage_error), so the run fails loudly and does not load the laptop; only the message is less helpful. The parsing is right for `-rx`, `-rsx`, `-srx`, `--maxfail 2` (its value is skipped as a test path) and node ids. Untested forms: `-xvs` (the second case pattern), `-n4`/`-nauto`, `--numprocesses`, `--ff`, `--sw-skip`. Accept or add params.", "files": ["scripts/test.sh", "tests/test_test_sh_script.py"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "pool-only needs a coordinator at 0.45.1 or later, and CI would read a refused manifest as a failure, not as an outage", "recommendation": "Confirm before merge that the coordinator runs 0.45.1 or later (the local client is 0.45.1). Per the guide, an older coordinator refuses a manifest naming `fallback`. ci-unit-pool.sh's classify counts bad_manifest as `failed`, so the check would go red instead of falling back to the shards. CI already passes --no-fallback, so once versions match, pool-only changes nothing on CI's route.", "files": [".testament.toml", "scripts/ci-unit-pool.sh"], "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "Callers and loop_timing coverage were checked, and nothing was lost", "recommendation": "none: check-all.sh calls test.sh with no arguments (no -x, -n or -m), so it is never refused. When the pool cannot take the run, check-all now stops at its test step with exit 2 instead of running the suite locally, which is the intended change. No workflow calls test.sh. loop_timing still runs on CI's pool route (ci-unit-tests.sh --loop-timing) and on its shard route (`rest`), and a local whole-suite run still runs them serially. Only a developer's pool run drops them, as intended. A loop_timing file named on the pool is now deselected, so testament exits 5. The named-file local route at test.sh:183 asks for no TESTAMENT_OFF_REASON but prints its own reason, the same pattern as the env-gate route. testament itself ran these runs locally before this change, so no reason gate is needed. The CHANGELOG claim about CI's integration job matches ci.yml (core, nats, epoch, scheduled-jobs, agent/acl). docs/testing.md:61's '-n 0 for the whole suite' sits under the 'none of the above applies' framing.", "files": ["scripts/check-all.sh", "scripts/test.sh", "docs/testing.md"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "No recorded test evidence", "recommendation": "prawduct-hook test-status reports stale because .prawduct/.test-evidence.json is missing. That is no finding at the inner stage. The review ran tests/test_test_sh_script.py once: 55 passed.", "oid": "O-7"}], "duration_seconds": 600, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "unbound", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `chore/pool-only`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": ["CHANGELOG.md", "CLAUDE.md", "docs/testing.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unch